{"type": "messages", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the isolated protocol-planner worker in Research World. Obey the supplied evidence and role boundary. Return one JSON object and no prose."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Design an executable wet-lab protocol proposal for one supplied claim. Docker cannot produce biological observations, so do not invent results. Return {\"claim_index\":int,\"hypothesis\":str,\"samples\":str,\"perturbations\":[str],\"controls\":[str],\"endpoints\":[str],\"analysis_plan\":str,\"stopping_rules\":[str],\"manual_result_schema\":{str:str},\"safety_and_ethics\":[str],\"cannot_establish_without_execution\":str}.\nINPUT:\n{\"direction\": {\"title\": \"Human immune-cell perturbation platform\", \"rationale\": \"Establishes a high-fidelity ex vivo and organoid-based experimental framework to directly manipulate human immune networks, bypassing species-specific translational gaps inherent in animal models.\", \"workflow\": \"wet_lab_proposal\", \"completion_test\": \"A validated standard operating procedure for multi-parameter single-cell readouts post-perturbation, complete with dose-response matrices, viability controls, and predefined success thresholds for signaling fidelity.\", \"remaining\": \"IRB clearance, patient sample procurement, and bench-scale protocol validation.\", \"position\": 0}, \"claims\": {\"claims\": [{\"node_id\": \"node:177ed12d69b18d71697ec7720cdf6f6a\", \"text\": \"In synthetic hydrogel-based lymphoid organoids, peripheral blood mononuclear cell (PBMC)-derived constructs will demonstrate statistically significant prolongation of germinal center B-cell and plasma-cell maintenance compared to tonsil-derived equivalents under identical culture conditions.\", \"kind\": \"prediction\", \"source_ids\": [\"source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a\"], \"scope\": \"Comparative longevity analysis of PBMC versus tonsil-derived B-cell lymphoid organoids in standardized hydrogel matrices\", \"rebuttal\": {\"claim_index\": 0, \"challenge\": \"The claim overlooks substantial donor-to-donor immunological variability and ex vivo expansion artifacts that can artificially prolong cell survival independent of tissue origin, while lacking the required viability controls and statistical power to substantiate 'statistically significant' differences.\", \"repair\": \"Restrict scope to donor-matched comparative cohorts within a single hydrogel batch, implement rigorous viability normalization against fresh primary isolates, and mandate pre-study power calculations alongside standardized survival curves before asserting significance.\"}}, {\"node_id\": \"node:130b7378ba0085b3b2ac628b75205964\", \"text\": \"Anti-CD20 immunotherapy in lymphoid organ-on-chip systems imposes a hard functional bound on germinal center formation capacity in lymphoma patient-derived B cells, preventing rescue via polarized CXCL12 microenvironmental gradients.\", \"kind\": \"bound\", \"source_ids\": [\"source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a\"], \"scope\": \"Therapeutic intervention limits on lymphoma patient B-cell germinal center dynamics within gradient-modulated organ-on-chip platforms\", \"rebuttal\": {\"claim_index\": 1, \"challenge\": \"Characterizing the anti-CD20 effect as a 'hard functional bound' overstates the mechanism, as therapeutic depletion may spare transitional/memory subsets or allow residual niche retention; additionally, the claim omits critical missing observations regarding anti-CD20 dosing kinetics and CXCL12 gradient concentration thresholds needed to prove absolute non-rescue.\", \"repair\": \"Reframe the assertion as a conditional suppression threshold dependent on specific drug concentrations and gradient intensities, incorporate healthy donor B-cell baselines to isolate disease-specific impairment, and define explicit rescue failure criteria based on quantitative GC architecture metrics.\"}}, {\"node_id\": \"node:02a59a61ec4bf1b7fe80814c00178524\", \"text\": \"Concurrent chemical inhibition of EZH2 and BCL6 transcriptional regulators in PBMC-derived hydrogel organoids will produce a quantifiable increase in terminal plasma cell differentiation rates exceeding single-target epigenetic blockade thresholds.\", \"kind\": \"hypothesis\", \"source_ids\": [\"source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a\"], \"scope\": \"Epigenetic and transcriptional co-inhibition efficacy in enhancing plasma cell generation within human B-cell organoid models\", \"rebuttal\": {\"claim_index\": 2, \"challenge\": \"Concurrent EZH2 and BCL6 inhibition introduces high risk of off-target cytotoxicity and aberrant lineage commitment that could confound differentiation readouts, while the claim ignores missing observations on transcriptional feedback loops and lacks single-agent dose-response baselines required to mathematically verify synergistic exceedance of thresholds.\", \"repair\": \"Integrate viability-corrected lineage tracing assays, standardize inhibitor administration windows relative to germinal center induction, and apply formal synergy quantification models (e.g., Bliss independence or Chou-Talalay) using rigorously titrated single-target controls to validate combined efficacy.\"}}], \"rebuttal\": {\"rebuttals\": [{\"claim_index\": 0, \"challenge\": \"The claim overlooks substantial donor-to-donor immunological variability and ex vivo expansion artifacts that can artificially prolong cell survival independent of tissue origin, while lacking the required viability controls and statistical power to substantiate 'statistically significant' differences.\", \"repair\": \"Restrict scope to donor-matched comparative cohorts within a single hydrogel batch, implement rigorous viability normalization against fresh primary isolates, and mandate pre-study power calculations alongside standardized survival curves before asserting significance.\"}, {\"claim_index\": 1, \"challenge\": \"Characterizing the anti-CD20 effect as a 'hard functional bound' overstates the mechanism, as therapeutic depletion may spare transitional/memory subsets or allow residual niche retention; additionally, the claim omits critical missing observations regarding anti-CD20 dosing kinetics and CXCL12 gradient concentration thresholds needed to prove absolute non-rescue.\", \"repair\": \"Reframe the assertion as a conditional suppression threshold dependent on specific drug concentrations and gradient intensities, incorporate healthy donor B-cell baselines to isolate disease-specific impairment, and define explicit rescue failure criteria based on quantitative GC architecture metrics.\"}, {\"claim_index\": 2, \"challenge\": \"Concurrent EZH2 and BCL6 inhibition introduces high risk of off-target cytotoxicity and aberrant lineage commitment that could confound differentiation readouts, while the claim ignores missing observations on transcriptional feedback loops and lacks single-agent dose-response baselines required to mathematically verify synergistic exceedance of thresholds.\", \"repair\": \"Integrate viability-corrected lineage tracing assays, standardize inhibitor administration windows relative to germinal center induction, and apply formal synergy quantification models (e.g., Bliss independence or Chou-Talalay) using rigorously titrated single-target controls to validate combined efficacy.\"}]}, \"review\": {\"findings\": [{\"check_id\": \"CITE-CONTEXT\", \"severity\": \"major\", \"evidence\": [{\"id\": \"source-snapshot:e7d9528c8ec67265fdf076e446fd7cee359584dba60e41868edae3d418927d4a\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 525}, \"sha256\": \"70d20034e09f95f1c3cea9f4e5ecc43004fe3373bf32d1f6ff7503dfff2334c3\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:4d9edaa447a746aa39ddc3a645e81517c7b755fe46dcdec3c9c9db6bae3d6816\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 2}, \"sha256\": \"af0044a18d0ca8e3a261765db22b9675dbeeaacd2322089a3b6feff0e50765a6\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 704}, \"sha256\": \"f8046f04a867c75a6c3a4809a52dc55bd000d157d1bfdaf79846b84811932785\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:08861704d4587675cc21542e4702b386a05f9ec022534d0dc4e7bfc9a568731d\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 580}, \"sha256\": \"75e1b7dfc452d67e98ba1a00c26ae20f009951bdaf815ea385eeffda5465aaf\"}], \"recommendation\": \"Retrieve full-text versions or substitute with accessible primary literature detailing wet-lab SOPs, dose-response validation, and multi-parameter single-cell readout protocols to substantiate the proposed framework.\"}, {\"check_id\": \"SCOPE-INFLATE\", \"severity\": \"major\", \"evidence\": [{\"id\": \"source-snapshot:e7d9528c8ec67265fdf076e446fd7cee359584dba60e41868edae3d418927d4a\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 525}, \"sha256\": \"70d20034e09f95f1c3cea9f4e5ecc43004fe3373bf32d1f6ff7503dfff2334c3\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 704}, \"sha256\": \"f8046f04a867c75a6c3a4809a52dc55bd000d157d1bfdaf79846b84811932785\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:08861704d4587675cc21542e4702b386a05f9ec022534d0dc4e7bfc9a568731d\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 580}, \"sha256\": \"75e1b7dfc452d67e98ba1a00c26ae20f009951bdaf815ea385eeffda5465aaf\"}], \"recommendation\": \"Narrow the directional scope to align with available evidence (e.g., B-cell lymphoid organoids and mass cytometry profiling) or acquire broader immunological perturbation data before claiming comprehensive immune network manipulation.\"}, {\"check_id\": \"RESULT-ARTIFACT-MISMATCH\", \"severity\": \"major\", \"evidence\": [{\"id\": \"source-snapshot:e7d9528c8ec67265fdf076e446fd7cee359584dba60e41868edae3d418927d4a\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 525}, \"sha256\": \"70d20034e09f95f1c3cea9f4e5ecc43004fe3373bf32d1f6ff7503dfff2334c3\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:4d9edaa447a746aa39ddc3a645e81517c7b755fe46dcdec3c9c9db6bae3d6816\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 2}, \"sha256\": \"af0044a18d0ca8e3a261765db22b9675dbeeaacd2322089a3b6feff0e50765a6\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 704}, \"sha256\": \"f8046f04a867c75a6c3a4809a52dc55bd000d157d1bfdaf79846b84811932785\"}, {\"id\": \"source-snapshot:08861704d4587675cc21542e4702b386a05f9ec022534d0dc4e7bfc9a568731d\", \"locator\": {\"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 580}, \"sha256\": \"75e1b7dfc452d67e98ba1a00c26ae20f009951bdaf815ea385eeffda5465aaf\"}], \"recommendation\": \"Develop and document the required SOP, dose-response matrices, and viability controls internally prior to submission, as current sources provide zero procedural validation or threshold definitions.\"}], \"summary\": \"The proposed platform's rationale overstates its breadth relative to the narrow, largely inaccessible evidence base, which consists primarily of metadata, a paywalled abstract focused on B-cell organoids, and one extraction failure. Furthermore, the completion test mandates validated SOPs, dose-response matrices, and signaling thresholds that are entirely absent from the provided materials. Substantive full-text literature or internal experimental documentation is required to validate the workflow, and the scope must be narrowed to match the available B-cell-centric data before the direction can be admitted.\"}}}"}]}
{"type": "model_output", "text": "{\n  \"claim_index\": 2,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Concurrent chemical inhibition of EZH2 and BCL6 in PBMC-derived hydrogel organoids will yield a statistically significant, viability-corrected increase in terminal plasma cell differentiation rates that mathematically exceeds the additive thresholds predicted by single-target epigenetic blockade alone.\",\n  \"samples\": \"Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) isolated from healthy adult donors, expanded ex vivo, and embedded in standardized synthetic PEG-fibrinogen hydrogels to form B-cell lymphoid organoids under defined germinal center induction conditions.\",\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    \"EZH2-specific small molecule inhibitor (titrated dose-response)\",\n    \"BCL6-specific small molecule inhibitor (titrated dose-response)\",\n    \"Concurrent dual inhibition at matched molar ratios across the dose matrix\"\n  ],\n  \"controls\": [\n    \"Vehicle control (DMSO equivalent)\",\n    \"Single-agent EZH2 inhibition at identical concentrations\",\n    \"Single-agent BCL6 inhibition at identical concentrations\",\n    \"Fresh primary PBMC baseline (day 0 viability and phenotype)\"\n  ],\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    \"Terminal plasma cell frequency (CD19- CD27high CD38high) via flow cytometry\",\n    \"Germinal center architectural integrity (area/volume fraction)\",\n    \"Cell viability and proliferation index (CFSE/Ki-67)\",\n    \"Transcriptional output (PRDM1, XBP1, IRF4 mRNA/protein levels)\",\n    \"Phospho-signaling readouts for downstream BCR/TGF-beta pathways\"\n  ],\n  \"analysis_plan\": \"Generate full dose-response matrices for all perturbations. Normalize all differentiation endpoints to day-0 fresh isolates and correct for compound-induced cytotoxicity. Calculate synergy indices using Bliss Independence and Chou-Talalay models. Compare dual-inhibition outcomes against single-agent curves using two-way ANOVA with Bonferroni correction. Apply pre-study power calculations to confirm statistical significance before finalizing conclusions.\",\n  \"stopping_rules\": [\n    \"Terminate experiment if overall viability drops below 60% at any timepoint\",\n    \"Abort dose escalation if IC50 shifts indicate non-specific membrane disruption\",\n    \"Cease cohort expansion if donor-matched variability exceeds predefined CV thresholds (>15%)\",\n    \"Stop if no measurable GC structure forms by day 7 regardless of treatment\"\n  ],\n  \"manual_result_schema\": {\n    \"donor_id\": \"string\",\n    \"hydrogel_batch_id\": \"string\",\n    \"treatment_condition\": \"string\",\n    \"concentration_nM\": \"number\",\n    \"days_in_culture\": \"integer\",\n    \"viability_percent\": \"number\",\n    \"plasma_cell_frequency_percent\": \"number\",\n    \"gc_architecture_score\": \"number\",\n    \"bliss_synergy_index\": \"number\",\n    \"chou_talalay_ci\": \"number\",\n    \"prdm1_fold_change\": \"number\"\n  },\n  \"safety_and_ethics\": [\n    \"IRB-approved informed consent for human peripheral blood collection\",\n    \"Adherence to BSL-2 laboratory practices for human cell culture\",\n    \"Proper handling and disposal of cytotoxic small-molecule inhibitors per institutional EHS guidelines\",\n    \"De-identification of all donor samples and compliance with HIPAA/GDPR data protection standards\"\n  ],\n  \"cannot_establish_without_execution\": \"Computational environments and dry-lab simulations cannot replicate the complex biophysical constraints of hydrogel matrices, dynamic cytokine gradients, or real-time epigenetic-transcriptional crosstalk required to validate synergistic plasma cell differentiation; empirical wet-lab execution with multi-parameter single-cell readouts is strictly necessary.\"\n}", "tool_calls": [], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 3514, "total_tokens": 6681, "completion_tokens": 3167, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 2331, "text_tokens": 3167}}, "model": "qwen3.7-flash"}
