itment that could confound differentiation readouts, while the claim ignores missing observations on transcriptional feedback loops and lacks single-agent dose-response baselines required to mathematically verify synergistic exceedance of thresholds.", "repair": "Integrate viability-corrected lineage tracing assays, standardize inhibitor administration windows relative to germinal center induction, and apply formal synergy quantification models (e.g., Bliss independence or Chou-Talalay) using rigorously titrated single-target controls to validate combined efficacy."}}], "rebuttal": {"rebuttals": [{"claim_index": 0, "challenge": "The claim overlooks substantial donor-to-donor immunological variability and ex vivo expansion artifacts that can artificially prolong cell survival independent of tissue origin, while lacking the required viability controls and statistical power to substantiate 'statistically significant' differences.", "repair": "Restrict scope to donor-matched comparative cohorts within a single hydrogel batch, implement rigorous viability normalization against fresh primary isolates, and mandate pre-study power calculations alongside standardized survival curves before asserting significance."}, {"claim_index": 1, "challenge": "Characterizing the anti-CD20 effect as a 'hard functional bound' overstates the mechanism, as therapeutic depletion may spare transitional/memory subsets or allow residual niche retention; additionally, the claim omits critical missing observations regarding anti-CD20 dosing kinetics and CXCL12 gradient concentration thresholds needed to prove absolute non-rescue.", "repair": "Reframe the assertion as a conditional suppression threshold dependent on specific drug concentrations and gradient intensities, incorporate healthy donor B-cell baselines to isolate disease-specific impairment, and define explicit rescue failure criteria based on quantitative GC architecture metrics."}, {"claim_index": 2, "challenge": "Concurrent EZH2 and BCL6 inhibition introduces high risk of off-target cytotoxicity and aberrant lineage commitment that could confound differentiation readouts, while the claim ignores missing observations on transcriptional feedback loops and lacks single-agent dose-response baselines required to mathematically verify synergistic exceedance of thresholds.", "repair": "Integrate viability-corrected lineage tracing assays, standardize inhibitor administration windows relative to germinal center induction, and apply formal synergy quantification models (e.g., Bliss independence or Chou-Talalay) using rigorously titrated single-target controls to validate combined efficacy."}]}, "review": {"findings": [{"check_id": "CITE-CONTEXT", "severity": "major", "evidence": [{"id": "source-snapshot:e7d9528c8ec67265fdf076e446fd7cee359584dba60e41868edae3d418927d4a", "locator": {"line_start": 1, "line_end": 525}, "sha256": "70d20034e09f95f1c3cea9f4e5ecc43004fe3373bf32d1f6ff7503dfff2334c3"}, {"id": "source-snapshot:4d9edaa447a746aa39ddc3a645e81517c7b755fe46dcdec3c9c9db6bae3d6816", "locator": {"line_start": 1, "line_end": 2}, "sha256": "af0044a18d0ca8e3a261765db22b9675dbeeaacd2322089a3b6feff0e50765a6"}, {"id": "source-snapshot:9fe214bb4a026b0310437b977b53d875eeadf12eea2401c60fa54ee50ff5e39a", "locator": {"line_start": 1, "line_end": 704}, "sha256": "f8046f04a867c75a6c3a4809a52dc55bd000d157d1bfdaf79846b84811932785"}, {"id": "source-snapshot:08861704d4587675cc21542e4702b386a05f9ec022534d0dc4e7bfc9a568731d", "locator": {"line_start": 1, "line_end": 580}, "sha256": "75e1b7dfc452d67e98ba1a00c26ae20f009951bdaf815ea385eeffda5465aaf"}], "recommendation": "Retrieve full-text versions or substitute with accessible primary literature detailing wet-lab SOPs, dose-response validation, and multi-parameter single-cell readout protocols to substantiate the proposed framework."}, {"check_id": "SCOPE-INFLATE", "severity": "major", "evidence": [{"id": "source-snapshot:e7d9528c8ec67265fdf076e446fd7cee359584dba60e41868edae3d